/Title (The global energy sector plays an important role in the economic growth and development of countries. Fuel is one of the most essential commodities because it is widely used in transportation, industries, agriculture, and everyday life. Changes in fuel prices directly affect the cost of living, transportation expenses, production costs, and the overall economy. Fuel taxation policies also differ from country to country, making it important to understand how these differences influence fuel prices across the world.)
